{"kind":"request","text":"Design the public application installation, checker-deployment and evolution seams\n\nBuilder/design: deliver notes/2026-10-03-application-installation.md with public-package/Room/operator deployment diagram and authority table. Separate application declarations/ordinary acts, admin policy activation, operator service-binding provisioning and package/Worker deployment. Use actual supported same-account checker route initially and name who provisions it for a hosted outsider. Coordinate existing f12cef6b job-authority contract and stage4 48c021ea v2 job dispatch; neither is cross-account transport delivery. Determine whether an actual next task needs HTTPS signed jobs or pull; if needed propose exact authenticated/replay/read-token/revocation/cleanup contract and separate runtime lanes, otherwise retain a named owner/trigger for that later gap. Keep independent actor validator review distinct from machine checking.\n\nCommissioned under independently approved experience map a259c26d and adopted scope cf116410, planned at main e6e6782830e0ca8a68f0d11c4d4ece5e4e98c967. This request delivers the design/specification and implementing-lane handoff. Planner will commission its implementation separately after exact design review and adoption; no new protocol/runtime decision is adopted here.\n\nJam section9, stage5/history/replay and f12cef6b/48c021ea owners. N3 uses the actual chosen provisioning path. Builder chooses blockers against the concrete next task.","body":{"conditions":"Specify one honest worked policy/act update: dry-run/read capabilities classified delivered versus missing, exact activation, deliberate regrant/new intent, stale intent refusal, retained old history and incompatible release behavior. Identify missing policy reads/dry-run contract dependencies rather than inventing public methods. Outsider installs/updates through public interfaces plus explicit operator/admin steps, sees useful configuration failure and knows deployment